course: dictionary
lesson: 6428
title: Myoglobin, the oxygen store in muscles
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Muscles need oxygen to keep working, and blood carries it to them. Myoglobin is a protein inside muscles that holds oxygen until the muscle needs it. Think of it as a small oxygen tank kept ready inside the muscle.
explain: Myoglobin is also red, which is why it changes the colour of meat. Muscles that work hard for a long time have more of it. «Dark meat has more myoglobin, a red protein that stores oxygen in muscles that work for a long time.» So the parts of an animal that keep working for hours are darker.
explain: Whales and seals use myoglobin to hold their breath for a long time. Their muscles store a lot of oxygen, so they can stay under water without coming up for air. Always check: does your answer fit the clue in the text?
fact: Myoglobin is a protein found in muscles.
fact: Myoglobin holds oxygen until the muscle needs it.
fact: Myoglobin is red, so muscles with a lot of it look dark red or dark.
fact: «Dark meat has more myoglobin» because those muscles work for a long time.
fact: Whales and seals have a lot of myoglobin, which helps them hold their breath under water.
exercise: What does myoglobin do? | It carries blood around the body | *It holds oxygen in muscles until the muscle needs it | It makes bones strong | It digests food in the stomach
exercise: «A chicken's legs are dark and its breast is pale.» Why are the legs darker? | The legs are painted | The legs are older than the breast | The legs have less blood | *The leg muscles work for a long time and store more myoglobin
exercise: The text says «ducks and wild pigeons that fly a lot have dark breast meat.» Which bird has dark breast meat? | *A wild pigeon that flies a lot | A goose that stays on the pond | A chicken, whose breast is pale | A bird that never flies
test: Whales can stay under water for a long time. What helps them do this? | Their large tails | Loud songs | *Myoglobin in their muscles, which stores oxygen | Their smooth skin
test: Which muscles would probably have the most myoglobin? | Muscles that only work for one second | Muscles that never move | Muscles in the ears | *Muscles that work hard for a long time
exam: Why is the meat from a duck's breast darker than a chicken's breast? Use the word myoglobin in your answer. | *Duck breast muscles work for a long time, so they store more myoglobin | Ducks have no muscles in their breast | Chickens are painted pale | Ducks eat more berries
